  "project": "madelon-reanalysis",
  "reason": "A correction to rev-1, whose two floor resolutions named the wrong methods. The measures of live-1 step-18 and live-2 step-19 do meet the criteria of floor-l1 and floor-forest, and a map checks criteria, not methods, so both errors passed check; reading the code each trail ran found them. live-1 ran (step-17, snapshot 13a6623) a search over six model families with SelectKBest inside cross-validation; its output names a random forest on 20 selected features as the best configuration. live-2 ran (step-18, snapshot 1763011) SelectKBest of 30 features inside cross-validation, then a random forest of 100 trees. Neither used L1, and neither used a forest on all 500 features. This revision withdraws both resolutions, adds the routes search and selected-forest with the nodes those steps do reach, and returns l1 and forest to open: no trail has walked them. The goal floor stays reached. The two trails converged on one design, a forest on 20 to 30 features selected inside cross-validation, which is the screened-forest route to compact; neither measured n_features, so compact stays open. live-1's output also gives each family's best inner cross-validated AUC: random forest 0.7198, k-nearest neighbours 0.6625, gradient boosting 0.6564, SVM 0.6488, logistic 0.6432. They are printed, not measured into the metrics file, so the map does not use them, but they say where a run toward compact is most likely to arrive: screened-forest.",
